id: high-sky
name: High Sky
kind: high
highRank: 2
noWeather: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Above the clouds. No Battle Weather can exist up here.
text: >
  High Sky Environment: Above the clouds, with space hanging above.

  Hardness Rank: N/A

  Effects: Battle Weather cannot exist in this Battle Environment.

---

# "Battle Weather cannot exist in this Battle Environment."
#
# `noWeather: true`, read by the registry: the Weather the character is standing in is not
# gathered while they are up here. Left on them rather than cleared, the same way the
# Battle Environment below is - the storm is still there when they come down.
#
# Cannot exist, so this is not a Weather Tier reduced to nothing. Brace's `weather.tiers`
# says Weathers count some number of Tiers lower and is a different rule; this says there
# is no Weather here at all, and a Tier of nothing would still be a Weather with a name.
#
# The first of the three that say it, and the reason the line is drawn here: below the
# clouds is where weather happens.
#
# No statements. What this does is refuse something, and refusing is the registry's.
